    "turn_text": "hello there kervis we've made it a year a year i can't even believe this podcast has been live for a year already this is crazy to me this is jimmy from flintstone media year host and producer of curve the cube and i am so grateful so grateful to have made it this far and i'm still looking forward to everything that's coming in the future for this podcast. So I just want to say a big, big, big thank you to all of my listeners. New and old, the ones who started with me from the very beginning and the ones who were just just coming on board. Thank you to all of you. You've really helped this podcast grow. and thank you to everyone who follows Curve the Cube on social media, we're on Twitter, on Facebook, Instagram, and now on YouTube. So follow, like, subscribe, and on YouTube in particular, please be sure to leave comments for feedback that way we get higher up in those rankings that are so important. But thank you, I cannot thank you enough. Thank you to my friends, to my family for everyone's support. In particular, I want to say thank you to my sponsors. We have, let's see, Little Smiles, The Pizza Girls, No Hard Feelings, Tattoo Shops, Soul Experiences, and our newest sponsor, Janice Massey-Salon. Look them all up, you can go to Curve the Cube onto our sponsor page and find links and all their info. to find all our great sponsors. Thank you, thank you, thank you to all of them for supporting, continuing to support us. And if you're interested in becoming a sponsor, all that info is right there on the website as well. Thank you, also a big thanks to two friends in particular who have really been amazing cheerleaders for me. My pod squad, Scotty Fusion and Jason Tron, they've been such wonderful assets for me. So thank you to them. Look for their individual episodes. They have great episodes, super funny, super great guys, along with our Paw Squad episodes, which we were continuing to deliver to you. So far we have two episodes out, one about the 80s was super fun, and one to get you in the hallways. Spirits all spooky and stuff so all about Halloween so go find that one as well and To so just a big thank you to everyone because this podcast wouldn't happen Without I mean it takes serious blood-swend tears for myself, but it wouldn't happen It wouldn't be a podcast without my listeners and my sponsors and my friends and just the incredible support that I've had so thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you and I want to encourage everyone to catch up with old episodes on all kinds of places. Let's see, well, curvethecube.com, obviously, on Stitcher, Player FM, Libsyn, on iTunes, and on the TuneIn app, wherever you can find it. Catch up on old episodes, because the whole point of this podcast is to inspire people to pursue your passions and your dreams, and every episode aims to do just that with some incredible guests. So don't miss any of them. Catch up, catch up, catch up. In fact, in the episode that is featured today, this anniversary episode, I referenced a previous episode that I really want to encourage everyone to go back and listen to in particular. It's episode over 33 with my friend Drew who really goes into the realities and struggles of transgender life. So go find episode 33 with my friend Drew. In this episode, episode number 47, my anniversary episode, I still can't even believe that this even happened to me this morning. I'm just flabbergasted and still beside myself, but it's with Congresswoman Lois Frankel, who has been just such a wonderful advocate for the common man. She has been a fighter for people's rights, for equal rights, for equality, for justice. um forever for decades she's been doing this she's been in public service for so long she's she's done um she was in the florida house representatives she was mayor of west palm beach and now she's representing florida district 22 in the u.s house of representatives and she's just an incredible woman incredible congresswoman and i'm just so thankful that she took the time to sit down with me and she goes into where her passions come from and she almost brought me to tears a couple of times she's just that inspirational and that incredible and I'm so proud and honored to have been able to have her on not just the podcast in general but to have her on in particular on my my anniversary episode it was just I'm I still can't even believe",
