    "turn_text": "as I said to her, you know, I may have seen calm cool and collected on the outside, but on the inside it was completely spazzing out. I was so happy to have been there. So her passion for what she does is just innate and it spills over and you're going to hear it come through the speakers on this podcast because she's just incredible. Wonderful, wonderful, wonderful. I cannot say enough. And this podcast is sponsored by Charity that is near and dear to my heart and also near and dear to hers, Little Smiles. You've heard me talk about them on previous podcasts, but I just can't say enough. Little Smiles does so much great work for kids in the community who need extra help, whether it's their house burned down and all their Christmas presents were lost or If they're struggling and they need something, a piece of equipment or special iPad for physical therapy or they're sick in the hospital and they just need someone to come and visit and little smiles just steps up in such amazing ways. So go to littlesmiles.org, please, I implore you. Donate, donate and donate in particular. Not if there's anything wrong with the other chapters but... I like to pay special attention to the Florida chapters also because they're always cool events going on. You can donate directly or you can attend an event and those are always great fundraisers for the charity. So I'm gonna stop blabbing now because I just really want you guys to be tuned into this episode. Episode number 47 and I still can't believe I'm saying it, but with Congressman Lois Frankel, this is Jimmy with Curve the Cube. Enjoy!",
